An error boundary wraps this component. What happens when the user clicks the button?

```jsx
function Save() {
  return (
    <button onClick={() => { throw new Error('save failed'); }}>
      Save
    </button>
  );
}
```

This app crashes with an error saying the lazy element type is invalid. Why, and what is the fix?

```jsx
// Chart.js
export function Chart() { /* ... */ }

// App.js
const Chart = lazy(() => import('./Chart'));
```

What does the user see right after typing a new character?

```jsx
function Search() {
  const [query, setQuery] = useState('a');
  const deferred = useDeferredValue(query);
  return (
    <>
      <input value={query} onChange={e => setQuery(e.target.value)} />
      <Suspense fallback={<Spinner />}>
        <Results query={deferred} />  {/* suspends on new queries */}
      </Suspense>
    </>
  );
}
```

What does this component show after `next()` is called, while `Data` for user 2 is still loading?

```jsx
function Profile() {
  const [id, setId] = useState(1);
  const [isPending, startTransition] = useTransition();
  const next = () => startTransition(() => setId(2));
  return (
    <div style={{ opacity: isPending ? 0.6 : 1 }}>
      <Suspense fallback={<Spinner />}>
        <Data id={id} />  {/* user 1 already loaded */}
      </Suspense>
    </div>
  );
}
```

Both apps call `startTransition(() => setTab('b'))`, and tab B's data is not loaded yet. What does each show while loading?

```jsx
// App 1
<Suspense fallback="Loading page">
  {tab === 'a' ? <TabA /> : <TabB />}         {/* TabB suspends */}
</Suspense>

// App 2
<Suspense fallback="Loading page">
  {tab === 'a' ? <TabA /> : (
    <section>
      <h2>Tab B</h2>
      <Suspense fallback="Loading B"><TabBData /></Suspense>
    </section>
  )}
</Suspense>
```

In React 19, an async action throws after an `await`. Where does the error go?

```jsx
function SaveButton() {
  const [isPending, startTransition] = useTransition();
  const save = () => startTransition(async () => {
    await api.save();          // rejects
  });
  return <button onClick={save}>{isPending ? 'Saving' : 'Save'}</button>;
}
// <ErrorBoundary fallback={<p>Failed</p>}><SaveButton /></ErrorBoundary>
```

React logs "A component was suspended by an uncached promise" for this component. Why is this a problem, and what is the fix?

```jsx
function Comments({ postId }) {
  const comments = use(fetch(`/api/comments/${postId}`).then(r => r.json()));
  return <List items={comments} />;
}
```

